0	121	TIMO PESONEN
Timo Pesonen is the current Director-General of DG 
Defence Industry and Space in the European Commission. 

121	280	After graduating in 1989 in International Politics from the University of Tampere, he 
stayed in his home country to serve at the Ministry for Foreign Affairs.
281	386	He then left for 
Brussels and the Embassy of Finland, where he worked with Foreign and Security policy.

386	549	The year 1995 marked his appointment to European Commission where he worked 
with foreign policy and as the spokesman for Commissioner Erkki Liikanen, 
1996-1997.

549	654	From 1997 to 2002, he served as Foreign Policy Adviser to the Prime Minister of 
Finland, Paavo Lipponen.
655	779	He also undertook an advisory mission during the Kosovo 
peace negotiations for the President of Finland, Martti Ahtisaari.

779	859	He acted as Head of Cabinet of Vice-President Olli Rehn for 10 years, 2004-2014.
860	964	He 
became Deputy Director-General of DG Communication in 2014 and Director-
General the following year.
965	1170	Taking the helm of DG Internal Market, Industry, 
Entrepreneurship and SMEs in March 2019, he accompanied the creation of DG 
Defence Industry and Space in 2020 as the head of the new Directorate-Gene
1170	1254	In addition to his native Finnish, Timo Pesonen speaks English, Swedish and French.

